WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.051
Markdown and MDX files
mix prose with code,

2
00:00:04.051 --> 00:00:07.998
imports, and frontmatter that a
compiler must still parse after

3
00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:08.868
translation.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.761
General Translation translates
the prose and keeps code,

5
00:00:12.761 --> 00:00:16.011
imports, and link URLs intact.

6
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.890
Translate alt text and
frontmatter titles too,

7
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.594
and quote translated YAML values.

8
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.422
Add an mdx entry under
files in gt.config.json.

9
00:00:27.822 --> 00:00:34.172
Then npx gt translate reads docs/en
and writes French and Japanese.

10
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.168
Run your site's build and link
checks on every locale before

11
00:00:38.168 --> 00:00:38.829
publishing.

12
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.110
Your team now ships
French with each release.
